    "result_text": "The only test class is the `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are its base and helper). The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for the `POST /api/owners` endpoint.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **Created a dedicated component** `OwnerCreationAuditLogger` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/OwnerCreationAuditLogger.java`) with a single responsibility: emitting the owner-creation audit line to the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`. This mirrors the existing pattern of small, focused collaborators in that package (e.g. `CustomerCodeAssigner`, `RegistrationDateAssigner`). Its `logCreated(Owner)` method logs the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n2. **Wired it into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected via the constructor and invoked once, right after `saveOwner(owner)` succeeds, so the id and derived fields are populated and the line is only emitted on a genuine successful create.\n\n**Why this placement:** The audit is a create-time side-effect that belongs with the other create-flow collaborators rather than inlined into the already-busy controller method or bolted onto an unrelated class. Keeping it in its own component keeps the controller thin and the logic reusable/testable in isolation.\n\nThe audit line format is:\n```\nAUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-18\n```\n`registrationDate` uses `LocalDate`'s ISO string, which matches the JSON representation the test reads back via `GET`, so `AuditLogCapture.anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` succeeds.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` and the full `mvn test` build both pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
